        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4d09b463-1c08-51ca-b7f8-21829045aa64",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sunye, Stephen Pearcy, Sohee, Hyuna, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani\n- Groups: Wonder Girls, Vertex, Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Roles: missionary, singer, actress, musician, guitarist, drummer\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956, and he is an American musician.\n- Sunye was born as Min Sun-ye on August 12, 1989, and she is a South Korean missionary and a former singer and actress on hiatus.\n- Vertex was a band formed in 1995 featuring singer Stephen Pearcy, guitarist Al Pitrelli, and drummer Hiro Kuretani.\n- Stephen Pearcy was associated with Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic.\n- Al Pitrelli was associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra.\n- Hiro Kuretani was associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station.\n- Wonder Girls member Hyuna left the group in late 2007.\n- Wonder Girls members Sunye and Sohee officially left the group in 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
